---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import HeroSection from '../../components/HeroSection.astro';
import CTABanner from '../../components/CTABanner.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Stadium Ceiling Maintenance & Construction"
  description="Crawler under-ceiling platforms for stadium roof access: acoustic panel installation, rigging, lighting grid work, and large-span structural maintenance. 20m–35m reach."
>

  <HeroSection
    variant="inner"
    title="Stadium Ceilings & Large-Span Roofs"
    subtitle="FDDPT crawler platforms for Olympic stadiums, sports arenas, and concert halls — work under the roof while the pitch stays clear."
    breadcrumb={[
      { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
      { name: 'Applications', url: '/applications/' },
      { name: 'Stadium Ceilings', url: '' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:800px;">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem;">Stadium Ceiling Challenges</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">Modern stadiums present unique ceiling access challenges. Roof spans of 100m+ sit 25m–70m above the field. Acoustic panels, lighting grids, rigging points, and HVAC systems all need installation and periodic maintenance — but scaffolding from the field level costs millions in lost event revenue and pitch damage.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:1rem;">The FDDPT series crawls directly onto the seating tiers or concourse deck, deploys its platform to the working height, and travels along the roof structure — without ever touching the pitch.</p>
      <p>A single FDDPT-35M can cover the same ceiling area in one week that would take scaffolding crews a month — while the venue remains operational below.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;text-align:center;margin-bottom:2rem;">Recommended Models for Stadium Work</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div style="padding:1.5rem;background:white;border-radius:0.75rem;border:1px solid var(--color-border);">
          <h3 style="font-weight:700;">FDDPT-35M — Flagship</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--color-text-light);margin:0.5rem 0;">For the tallest stadium roofs (30m+). 12m×8m platform covers massive ceiling sections per deployment. 3T load handles heavy acoustic panels and lighting arrays.</p>
          <a href="/products/fddpt-35m-crawler-ceiling-platform/" class="btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm mt-2">View Model</a>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:1.5rem;background:white;border-radius:0.75rem;border:1px solid var(--color-border);">
          <h3 style="font-weight:700;">FDDPT-31M — High-Reach</h3>
          <p style="color:var(--color-text-light);margin:0.5rem 0;">Balanced reach and maneuverability for typical arena roofs (25m–31m). Lighter than 35M, faster repositioning between bays. Ideal for seasonal maintenance cycles.</p>
          <a href="/products/fddpt-31m-crawler-ceiling-platform/" class="btn btn-outline-dark btn-sm mt-2">View Model</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABanner
    title="Planning stadium ceiling work?"
    subtitle="Tell us your roof height and access constraints — we'll spec the right FDDPT configuration."
    ctaText="Get a Project Assessment"
    ctaUrl="/contact/"
  />
</BaseLayout>
